            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "partograph_interpretation_subsection_9",
          "subsection_title": "How to present your final interpretation",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "partograph_interpretation_group_22",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Use this model answer when the examiner hands you a completed partograph:"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "“This is a partograph documenting the progress of labour in a woman at term. I would first confirm the patient's details, gestational age, parity, time of labour monitoring and the type of chart used."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "I would assess fetal well-being by reviewing the fetal heart rate, liquor and moulding. I would then assess labour progress by examining cervical dilatation, descent of the presenting part and uterine contractions. Finally, I would review maternal observations, including pulse, blood pressure, temperature and urine findings."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "I would determine whether labour is progressing appropriately and identify any abnormalities. If there is delayed progress, I would assess the powers, passenger and passage, while excluding obstruction. I would also assess for maternal or fetal compromise."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "My management would depend on the findings and could include continued monitoring, correction of reversible causes, appropriate augmentation when safe, or expedited birth if indicated. I would document the findings, seek senior review when necessary and explain the plan to the woman.”"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}